4c2-58ca-563f-a943-2b87144d054f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0130011a-855a-504c-8ed9-de640a85cf65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529577} {:answer/id #uuid "53308e85-0ea9-5376-ba91-1d38df29c1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529778} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb0e05e-e814-59a0-b300-e445fc5ab637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0130011a-855a-504c-8ed9-de640a85cf65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529577} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddb27815-0b88-5fe1-9bd9-3f33b06ca48a" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22670f3b-ee2e-505b-bc5c-db0616554dee" :question/math-academy-id "q-333345" :question/problem "![](images/51/51ffadb1da41e6a1fe06fdc9c14a6967d3a80b4d26c6a830a401105e0f18bbf5.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,2]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}.\n\nFinally, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector {{field-9}} as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is \n{{field-10}}.\n\nTherefore,\n{{field-11}} \n$<0.$" :question/worked-solution "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=-2x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/6e/6ea2d64a390187a28cfcd1c2692e97e5dc2ca5cb37649ba12cf71864e36958ea.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}<0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=2x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f2340cbff80765a5d3b551e87eb4207eebad05970e366ceeccd7bb142c0b677.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nSo, for this particular system, both eigenvalues are negative. The eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is the one closest to $0.$\n\nNow, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector ${v}_{1}$ as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior is ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\n\nTherefore, ${\\lambda }_{2}<{\\lambda }_{1}<0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13af6d27-628d-5bdb-b396-299d9cfd64e7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "513de073-e1bd-5a16-ab21-c12d64138eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305940} {:answer/id #uuid "56487585-95b8-5f3b-beb2-679116dd1144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305984} {:answer/id #uuid "d40e2872-fdd4-59fa-8d11-bb36610b8c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307118} {:answer/id #uuid "f064c541-8ed7-5191-b366-1d714dc5fb59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d40e2872-fdd4-59fa-8d11-bb36610b8c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} 