wer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "278cfbb6-56c7-5979-9623-cc2ac70af8e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305521} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd271e13-4b4d-504a-9f30-a5d43cb17574" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c833496-a809-5eea-acb1-bfc822315c03" :question/math-academy-id "q-333643" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n$y=-x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-2x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-2x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/45/450d43a4cbf6dad8d54edbb66fc4a6e44e491290e1dc5d1303057fb0eb7928a7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166918 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35492718-d2d7-5c9d-9c02-1ef6ae0445d0" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Distinct Real Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09127fa6-751e-5de5-9626-f7c3ade21701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529594} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbd7798-2750-5c2f-b9ba-11c058833061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09127fa6-751e-5de5-9626-f7c3ade21701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529594} :answer-field/id #uuid "52e5d219-347a-59f7-9240-fa2c72d0c7a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0adbae6f-09ad-5e85-adc2-3211170c6c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529597} {:answer/id #uuid "15eece98-8f78-5bc6-9ed2-aea0eb111e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #